Chapter 1: Introduction to Computer Networks
What is a Computer Network?

A computer network is a collection of two or more devices connected together so they can communicate and share resources.

Think of it as a group of people connected by phones. Instead of people talking to each other, computers exchange data.

Formal Definition

A computer network is a system that connects computers and other devices using communication links and protocols to exchange data and share resources.

Why Do We Need Networks?

Imagine there were no networks.

Suppose your college has:

100 computers
20 printers
One internet connection

Without networking:

Every computer would need its own printer.
Files would have to be copied using USB drives.
Internet could not be shared.
Collaboration would be difficult.

Networking solves these problems.

