Real-Life Examples
Example 1: Home Wi-Fi

Your home has:

Laptop
Mobile phone
Smart TV
Alexa
CCTV camera

All connect to the same Wi-Fi router.

This creates a Local Area Network (LAN).

When your laptop accesses the internet, the data travels through the router to your Internet Service Provider (ISP), then to the destination server, and the response comes back the same way.

Example 2: College Network

A college may have:

2,000 computers
Servers
Printers
Attendance system
Library system

All are connected through switches and routers.

Students can:

Access the library
Download notes
Use the internet
Print documents
Example 3: Banking

When you withdraw ₹500 from an ATM:

The ATM sends a request through a network.
The bank server checks your balance.
If sufficient funds are available, the transaction is approved.
The ATM dispenses cash.

Without networking, online banking and ATMs would not work.

