Networking and Cybersecurity

Networking is the foundation of cybersecurity.

As a SOC analyst, you'll regularly analyze:

Source and destination IP addresses
Port numbers
Network protocols (HTTP, DNS, TCP, etc.)
Firewall logs
Packet captures (PCAPs)
IDS/IPS alerts

Without understanding networking, it's difficult to investigate security incidents effectively.

Common Beginner Misconceptions

Q: Is the Internet the same as a network?
No. The Internet is a global network made up of millions of smaller networks.

Q: Can one computer be called a network?
No. A network requires at least two connected devices.

Q: Is Wi-Fi the Internet?
No. Wi-Fi is a wireless method of connecting devices to a network. You can have Wi-Fi without Internet access (for example, a local network for file sharing).
